steps.body:
The median is the middle value once the numbers are sorted. When numbers keep arriving, sorting again after each one costs O(n log n) every time. Two heaps keep the middle ready instead:

- `low` is a max-heap of the smaller half, built with `Collections.reverseOrder()`, so `low.peek()` is the biggest small number.
- `high` is a min-heap of the larger half, so `high.peek()` is the smallest big number.

To add `x`, offer it to `low`, move `low`'s top over to `high`, and if `high` is now bigger, move its top back:

```java harness
PriorityQueue<Integer> low = new PriorityQueue<>(Collections.reverseOrder());
PriorityQueue<Integer> high = new PriorityQueue<>();
for (int x : new int[]{5, 15, 1}) {
    {{code}}
}
System.out.println(low.peek() + " " + high.peek());
```

```java
low.offer(x);
high.offer(low.poll());      // the biggest small number moves up
if (high.size() > low.size()) {
    low.offer(high.poll());  // low keeps the extra one
}
```

Passing every number through `low` keeps all of `low` at or below all of `high`. The sizes never differ by more than one, and `low` holds the extra. So with an odd count the median is `low.peek()`, and with an even count it's the average of the two tops, `(low.peek() + high.peek()) / 2.0`. Divide by `2.0`, not `2`: two `int` values divide as integers and drop the half.

Each new number costs a few heap operations on heaps of about n / 2 items, so O(log n), and reading the median is O(1). The two heaps hold every number, O(n) space.

example.code:
import java.util.Collections;
import java.util.PriorityQueue;
import java.util.Scanner;

public class Main {
    public static void main(String[] args) {
        Scanner sc = new Scanner(System.in);
        int n = sc.nextInt();
        PriorityQueue<Integer> low = new PriorityQueue<>(Collections.reverseOrder());
        PriorityQueue<Integer> high = new PriorityQueue<>();
        for (int i = 0; i < n; i++) {
            String bidder = sc.next();
            int amount = sc.nextInt();
            low.offer(amount);
            high.offer(low.poll());
            if (high.size() > low.size()) {
                low.offer(high.poll());
            }
            double median;
            if (low.size() > high.size()) {
                median = low.peek();
            } else {
                median = (low.peek() + high.peek()) / 2.0;
            }
            System.out.printf("%s: median %.1f%n", bidder, median);
        }
    }
}

